<title>FINLAND: Outokumpu, Rautaruukki see metal prices up - paper.</title>
<headline>Outokumpu, Rautaruukki see metal prices up - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish steel group Rautaruukki Oy and base metals and mining group Outokumpu Oy expect metal prices to rise further this year, current affairs weekly Suomen Kuvalehti reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Metals prices have already bottomed out. A rise has been observed in Europe and elsewhere,&quot; Suomen Kuvalehti quoted Outokumpu CEO Jyrki Juusela as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;The cyclical situation resembles the situation in 1993, when a rise (in metals prices) started,&quot; Rautaruukki CEO Mikko Kivimaki was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>The price rise which started in 1993 lasted until late in 1995, he said, adding metals prices had now been on the rise since September 1996.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
